title: mf trash restore
tags: [[CLI command]] Trash
kind: reference
summary: Restore a trashed file to its original path

Puts the entry back: its metarecords first, then the bytes, at the path they were
trashed from ([[What restoring does]]). An occupied path is refused — move the
occupant aside first — except a directory, which is merged into an existing one
when no file would be overwritten.
